/// known-gap: interp has no block overlay syntax (overlay name ... xx); the interpreter is being retired
/// `link name` with `hosts:`, `range:` and `score` (default: the low end
/// of the range). `:link!(a, b, link, change)` moves a's link to b and
/// keeps it in its range; with ticks the change is taken back when they run
/// out. `:unlink!(a, b, link)` takes back every change.
<>K |
    faith: .5
xx
link culture
    hosts: K
    range: 0...1
    score => 1 - :abs((@faith) - (target >> faith))
xx
link trade
    hosts: K
    range: -10...10
xx
a <> K | faith: .2
b <> K | faith: .7
say(:link_score(a, b, culture))
say(:link_score(a, b, trade))
:link!(a, b, trade, 4)
say(:link_score(a, b, trade))
say(:link_score(b, a, trade))
:link!(a, b, trade, 30)
say(:link_score(a, b, trade))
:link!(a, b, culture, .25, 2)
say(:link_score(a, b, culture))
tick()
tick()
say(:link_score(a, b, culture))
:unlink!(a, b, trade)
say(:link_score(a, b, trade))
